IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g3-nouns`
IMPORT `g3-art8-register`
IMPORT `g3-fixtures`

-- g3-tests-art8-register.l4: tests of Article 8(1) to 8(3) -- the register, its sections, the status note and the fourteen items.
-- Every expected value is decided from the text of Article 8 (src:217-238) BEFORE the code was run; none was taken from the output.
-- A trace has no equality, so each #TRACE carries an EXPECT comment that check-traces.py reads.

§ `Tests of Article 8(1) to (3)`

fav MEANS `the favoured interpretation of Articles 8 to 10`

§§ `Article 8(1) and (2): the duties of the Commissioner`

-- 8(1): "must establish and maintain": it stands until the Commissioner does it; the Article states no time, so no deadline passes.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 8(1) the Commissioner must establish and maintain a register of charities` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `establish and maintain a register of charities` AT 3

-- EXPECT: STANDING | MUST `establish and maintain a register of charities`
#TRACE `Art 8(1) the Commissioner must establish and maintain a register of charities` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 4000)

-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 8(2) the register must be kept so as to distinguish between the general, restricted and historic sections` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `keep the register so as to distinguish between the general, restricted and historic sections` AT 3

-- EXPECT: STANDING | MUST `keep the register so as to distinguish between the general, restricted and historic sections`
#TRACE `Art 8(2) the register must be kept so as to distinguish between the general, restricted and historic sections` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 4000)

§§ `Article 8(2): the section as a function of the standing and of the day`

-- Registered charity (Article 1): the general or the restricted section, not the historic section.
#ASSERT `the standing is that of a registered charity` `entered in the general section`
#ASSERT `the standing is that of a registered charity` `entered in the restricted section`
#ASSERT NOT `the standing is that of a registered charity` `formerly registered and entered in the historic section`
#ASSERT NOT `the standing is that of a registered charity` `not on the register`
#ASSERT NOT `the standing is that of a registered charity` `an applicant for registration`

#ASSERT `the section named by the standing` `entered in the general section` EQUALS JUST `the general section`
#ASSERT `the section named by the standing` `entered in the restricted section` EQUALS JUST `the restricted section`
#ASSERT `the section named by the standing` `formerly registered and entered in the historic section` EQUALS JUST `the historic section`
#ASSERT `the section named by the standing` `not on the register` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the section named by the standing` `an applicant for registration` EQUALS NOTHING

-- A register history: entered in the general section on 1 March 2019, in the restricted section on 1 June 2021, in the historic section on 1 June 2024.
`the three placements` MEANS
    LIST (`a placement in` `the general section` `on` (YMD 2019 3 1)), (`a placement in` `the restricted section` `on` (YMD 2021 6 1)), (`a placement in` `the historic section` `on` (YMD 2024 6 1))

GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 8 to 10`
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE `Section of the register`
`the section on` interp day MEANS `Art 8(2) the section in which the entity is entered on` interp `the three placements` day

-- Before the first entry: in no section.
#ASSERT `the section on` fav (YMD 2019 2 28) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the section on` fav (YMD 2018 1 1) EQUALS NOTHING
-- The day of the entry (F3.6): the favoured reading takes effect on the day of the entry, the other on the day after.
#ASSERT `the section on` fav (YMD 2019 3 1) EQUALS JUST `the general section`
#ASSERT `the section on` `interpretation F3.6 reading B` (YMD 2019 3 1) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the section on` fav (YMD 2019 3 2) EQUALS JUST `the general section`
#ASSERT `the section on` `interpretation F3.6 reading B` (YMD 2019 3 2) EQUALS JUST `the general section`
-- Moving to the restricted section.
#ASSERT `the section on` fav (YMD 2021 5 31) EQUALS JUST `the general section`
#ASSERT `the section on` fav (YMD 2021 6 1) EQUALS JUST `the restricted section`
#ASSERT `the section on` `interpretation F3.6 reading B` (YMD 2021 6 1) EQUALS JUST `the general section`
#ASSERT `the section on` `interpretation F3.6 reading B` (YMD 2021 6 2) EQUALS JUST `the restricted section`
-- Deregistration: the historic section.
#ASSERT `the section on` fav (YMD 2024 5 31) EQUALS JUST `the restricted section`
#ASSERT `the section on` fav (YMD 2024 6 1) EQUALS JUST `the historic section`
#ASSERT `the section on` `interpretation F3.6 reading B` (YMD 2024 6 1) EQUALS JUST `the restricted section`
#ASSERT `the section on` `interpretation F3.6 reading B` (YMD 2024 6 2) EQUALS JUST `the historic section`
#ASSERT `the section on` fav (YMD 2030 1 1) EQUALS JUST `the historic section`
-- Two entries on the same day: the Law does not say which prevails, so the encoding takes the one listed later (the register's own order).  An assumption, not a reading of the text.
`two entries on 1 June 2021, general first` MEANS LIST (`a placement in` `the general section` `on` (YMD 2021 6 1)), (`a placement in` `the restricted section` `on` (YMD 2021 6 1))
`two entries on 1 June 2021, restricted first` MEANS LIST (`a placement in` `the restricted section` `on` (YMD 2021 6 1)), (`a placement in` `the general section` `on` (YMD 2021 6 1))
#ASSERT `Art 8(2) the section in which the entity is entered on` fav `two entries on 1 June 2021, general first` (YMD 2021 6 1) EQUALS JUST `the restricted section`
#ASSERT `Art 8(2) the section in which the entity is entered on` fav `two entries on 1 June 2021, restricted first` (YMD 2021 6 1) EQUALS JUST `the general section`
-- Never entered.
#ASSERT `Art 8(2) the section in which the entity is entered on` fav EMPTY (YMD 2026 1 1) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Article 8(3)(a): the note of the status of the entity`

-- A name for each sub-paragraph of Article 2(1).
`kind (a)` MEANS `the trustees of a trust`
`kind (b)` MEANS `the fidéicommissaires of a court-approved fidéicommis`
`kind (ba)` MEANS `a body corporate that is an NPO established under the law of Jersey`
`kind (c)` MEANS `an incorporated 1862 association`
`kind (d)` MEANS `a foundation`
`kind (e)` MEANS `a body corporate established by an enactment, an Act of the States or a Royal Charter`
`kind (f)` MEANS `a company`
`kind (g)` MEANS `a body incorporated under, but not by, an enactment other than the Companies (Jersey) Law 1991`
`kind (h)` MEANS `a body incorporated under, but not by, an Act of the United Kingdom Parliament or Order in Council`
`kind (i)` MEANS `an unincorporated body or association of persons`
`kind (j)` MEANS `an entity substantially similar to one of the above, established under the law of another jurisdiction`
`kind added by an Order` MEANS `an entity added by an Order under Article 2(2)` "(k)"

GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 8 to 10`
      ks IS A LIST OF `Kind of entity`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the answer to also within (a) for` interp ks MEANS (`Art 8(3)(a) the note of the status of the entity` interp (`an entity falling within` ks))'s `whether it also falls within sub-paragraph (a)`

GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 8 to 10`
      ks IS A LIST OF `Kind of entity`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Kind of entity`
`the kinds needing details for` interp ks MEANS (`Art 8(3)(a) the note of the status of the entity` interp (`an entity falling within` ks))'s `sub-paragraphs for which details of the enactment or foreign law are required`

-- 8(3)(a)(i): "in the case of an entity falling within one of sub-paragraphs (f) to (j) ..., whether it also falls within sub-paragraph (a)".
#ASSERT `the answer to also within (a) for` fav (LIST `kind (f)`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the answer to also within (a) for` fav (LIST `kind (g)`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the answer to also within (a) for` fav (LIST `kind (h)`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the answer to also within (a) for` fav (LIST `kind (i)`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the answer to also within (a) for` fav (LIST `kind (j)`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A company that is the sole trustee of a trust: sub-paragraphs (a) and (f).
#ASSERT `the answer to also within (a) for` fav (LIST `kind (a)`, `kind (f)`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the answer to also within (a) for` fav (LIST `kind (a)`, `kind (j)`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not within (f) to (j): no such statement is required.
#ASSERT `the answer to also within (a) for` fav (LIST `kind (a)`) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the answer to also within (a) for` fav (LIST `kind (b)`) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the answer to also within (a) for` fav (LIST `kind (c)`) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the answer to also within (a) for` fav (LIST `kind (d)`) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the answer to also within (a) for` fav (LIST `kind (e)`) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the answer to also within (a) for` fav (LIST `kind added by an Order`) EQUALS NOTHING

-- 8(3)(a)(ii): details for an entity within (e), (g), (h) or (j), and for no other.
#ASSERT `the kinds needing details for` fav (LIST `kind (e)`) EQUALS LIST `kind (e)`
#ASSERT `the kinds needing details for` fav (LIST `kind (g)`) EQUALS LIST `kind (g)`
#ASSERT `the kinds needing details for` fav (LIST `kind (h)`) EQUALS LIST `kind (h)`
#ASSERT `the kinds needing details for` fav (LIST `kind (j)`) EQUALS LIST `kind (j)`
#ASSERT `the kinds needing details for` fav (LIST `kind (a)`) EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `the kinds needing details for` fav (LIST `kind (b)`) EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `the kinds needing details for` fav (LIST `kind (c)`) EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `the kinds needing details for` fav (LIST `kind (d)`) EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `the kinds needing details for` fav (LIST `kind (f)`) EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `the kinds needing details for` fav (LIST `kind (i)`) EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `the kinds needing details for` fav (LIST `kind added by an Order`) EQUALS EMPTY
-- Two kinds: only those among them that need details.
#ASSERT `the kinds needing details for` fav (LIST `kind (a)`, `kind (g)`) EQUALS LIST `kind (g)`
#ASSERT `the kinds needing details for` fav (LIST `kind (e)`, `kind (f)`) EQUALS LIST `kind (e)`

-- Trap T5, F3.13: sub-paragraph (ba) is named by neither limb of Article 8(3)(a) (src:224-225).
-- A Jersey NPO body corporate within (ba) only: the note on the favoured reading says nothing about (a) and needs no details.
#ASSERT `the answer to also within (a) for` fav (LIST `kind (ba)`) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the kinds needing details for` fav (LIST `kind (ba)`) EQUALS EMPTY
-- The same entity that is also a trustee: no "also within (a)" statement on the favoured reading, a statement on the other.
#ASSERT `the answer to also within (a) for` fav (LIST `kind (ba)`, `kind (a)`) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the answer to also within (a) for` `interpretation F3.13 reading B` (LIST `kind (ba)`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the answer to also within (a) for` `interpretation F3.13 reading B` (LIST `kind (ba)`, `kind (a)`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the kinds needing details for` `interpretation F3.13 reading B` (LIST `kind (ba)`) EQUALS LIST `kind (ba)`
-- The other readings are not disturbed by F3.13.
#ASSERT `the answer to also within (a) for` `interpretation F3.13 reading B` (LIST `kind (f)`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the answer to also within (a) for` `interpretation F3.13 reading B` (LIST `kind (c)`) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the kinds needing details for` `interpretation F3.13 reading B` (LIST `kind (f)`) EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `the kinds needing details for` `interpretation F3.13 reading B` (LIST `kind (e)`) EQUALS LIST `kind (e)`

-- The note records the sub-paragraphs themselves, in the entity's own order.
#ASSERT (`Art 8(3)(a) the note of the status of the entity` fav (`an entity falling within` (LIST `kind (a)`, `kind (f)`)))'s `sub-paragraphs of Article 2(1) within which the entity falls` EQUALS LIST `kind (a)`, `kind (f)`

-- A recorded note is the note required if it records the same sub-paragraphs, the same answer on (a), and details wherever details are required.
`the requirement for a trust` MEANS `Art 8(3)(a) the note of the status of the entity` fav (`an entity falling within` (LIST `kind (a)`))
`the requirement for a body incorporated under an enactment` MEANS `Art 8(3)(a) the note of the status of the entity` fav (`an entity falling within` (LIST `kind (g)`))

`a note of a trust` MEANS
    `Note of status recorded in the register (Article 8(3)(a))` WITH
        `sub-paragraphs of Article 2(1) recorded` IS LIST `kind (a)`
        `whether it also falls within sub-paragraph (a), as recorded` IS NOTHING
        `details of the enactment, Act of the States, Royal Charter, Act of the United Kingdom Parliament, Order in Council or foreign law` IS NOTHING

`a note of a body incorporated under an enactment, with details` MEANS
    `Note of status recorded in the register (Article 8(3)(a))` WITH
        `sub-paragraphs of Article 2(1) recorded` IS LIST `kind (g)`
        `whether it also falls within sub-paragraph (a), as recorded` IS JUST FALSE
        `details of the enactment, Act of the States, Royal Charter, Act of the United Kingdom Parliament, Order in Council or foreign law` IS JUST "the Loi (1862) on the incorporation of associations"

`a note of a body incorporated under an enactment, without details` MEANS
    `Note of status recorded in the register (Article 8(3)(a))` WITH
        `sub-paragraphs of Article 2(1) recorded` IS LIST `kind (g)`
        `whether it also falls within sub-paragraph (a), as recorded` IS JUST FALSE
        `details of the enactment, Act of the States, Royal Charter, Act of the United Kingdom Parliament, Order in Council or foreign law` IS NOTHING

`a note of a body incorporated under an enactment, wrongly saying it is also a trust` MEANS
    `Note of status recorded in the register (Article 8(3)(a))` WITH
        `sub-paragraphs of Article 2(1) recorded` IS LIST `kind (g)`
        `whether it also falls within sub-paragraph (a), as recorded` IS JUST TRUE
        `details of the enactment, Act of the States, Royal Charter, Act of the United Kingdom Parliament, Order in Council or foreign law` IS JUST "an enactment"

#ASSERT `the recorded note of status is as Article 8(3)(a) requires` `the requirement for a trust` `a note of a trust`
#ASSERT `the recorded note of status is as Article 8(3)(a) requires` `the requirement for a body incorporated under an enactment` `a note of a body incorporated under an enactment, with details`
#ASSERT NOT `the recorded note of status is as Article 8(3)(a) requires` `the requirement for a body incorporated under an enactment` `a note of a body incorporated under an enactment, without details`
#ASSERT NOT `the recorded note of status is as Article 8(3)(a) requires` `the requirement for a body incorporated under an enactment` `a note of a body incorporated under an enactment, wrongly saying it is also a trust`
#ASSERT NOT `the recorded note of status is as Article 8(3)(a) requires` `the requirement for a trust` `a note of a body incorporated under an enactment, with details`

§§ `Article 8(3)(b): the names of the governors`

#ASSERT `Art 8(3)(b) the names of each of the governors to be entered` `a company in the general section` EQUALS LIST "Ann Le Brun", "Bob Renouf"
#ASSERT `Art 8(3)(b) the names of each of the governors to be entered` (`an entity falling within` (LIST `kind (f)`)) EQUALS LIST "Ann Le Brun", "Bob Renouf"

`an entity with a corporate trustee` MEANS
    Entity WITH
        name IS "Le Quesne Trust"
        `standing on the register` IS `entered in the general section`
        `kinds of entity` IS LIST `kind (a)`
        `is a Jersey entity` IS TRUE
        governors IS LIST `Jersey Trustees Limited`
        purposes IS EMPTY

`an entity with no governor yet` MEANS
    Entity WITH
        name IS "Le Quesne Trust"
        `standing on the register` IS `entered in the general section`
        `kinds of entity` IS LIST `kind (a)`
        `is a Jersey entity` IS TRUE
        governors IS EMPTY
        purposes IS EMPTY

-- A corporate trustee is a governor and its name is entered like any other.
#ASSERT `Art 8(3)(b) the names of each of the governors to be entered` `an entity with a corporate trustee` EQUALS LIST "Jersey Trustees Limited"
#ASSERT `Art 8(3)(b) the names of each of the governors to be entered` `an entity with no governor yet` EQUALS EMPTY

§§ `Article 8(3)(d): the addresses of other premises in Jersey`

GIVEN a IS A STRING
      jersey IS A BOOLEAN
      dwelling IS A BOOLEAN
      activity IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Premises of a charity (Articles 8(3)(d) and 8(4))`
`premises at` a `in Jersey` jersey `a private dwelling house` dwelling `with an activity` activity MEANS
    `Premises of a charity (Articles 8(3)(d) and 8(4))` WITH
        address IS a
        `in Jersey` IS jersey
        `a private dwelling house` IS dwelling
        `at or from which the charity undertakes an activity` IS activity

GIVEN ps IS A LIST OF `Premises of a charity (Articles 8(3)(d) and 8(4))`
      entered IS A MAYBE STRING
GIVETH A `Facts for the items of Article 8(3)`
`facts with other premises` ps `and the principal address entered` entered MEANS
    `Facts for the items of Article 8(3)` WITH
        `other premises` IS ps
        `principal address entered` IS entered
        `previous registered names` IS EMPTY
        `information prescribed by an Order under Article 8(3)(n)` IS EMPTY

-- Premises in Jersey, not a private dwelling house, where the charity undertakes an activity, and not the principal address.
#ASSERT `Art 8(3)(d) the addresses of other premises in Jersey to be entered` (`facts with other premises` (LIST `premises at` "1 Hill Street" `in Jersey` TRUE `a private dwelling house` FALSE `with an activity` TRUE) `and the principal address entered` (JUST "10 Library Place")) EQUALS LIST "1 Hill Street"
-- Each of the four exclusions on its own.
#ASSERT `Art 8(3)(d) the addresses of other premises in Jersey to be entered` (`facts with other premises` (LIST `premises at` "2 Elm Close" `in Jersey` TRUE `a private dwelling house` TRUE `with an activity` TRUE) `and the principal address entered` (JUST "10 Library Place")) EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `Art 8(3)(d) the addresses of other premises in Jersey to be entered` (`facts with other premises` (LIST `premises at` "5 Regent Street, London" `in Jersey` FALSE `a private dwelling house` FALSE `with an activity` TRUE) `and the principal address entered` (JUST "10 Library Place")) EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `Art 8(3)(d) the addresses of other premises in Jersey to be entered` (`facts with other premises` (LIST `premises at` "3 Pier Road" `in Jersey` TRUE `a private dwelling house` FALSE `with an activity` FALSE) `and the principal address entered` (JUST "10 Library Place")) EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `Art 8(3)(d) the addresses of other premises in Jersey to be entered` (`facts with other premises` (LIST `premises at` "10 Library Place" `in Jersey` TRUE `a private dwelling house` FALSE `with an activity` TRUE) `and the principal address entered` (JUST "10 Library Place")) EQUALS EMPTY
-- The premises at the principal address are "other" only if no principal address has been entered.
#ASSERT `Art 8(3)(d) the addresses of other premises in Jersey to be entered` (`facts with other premises` (LIST `premises at` "10 Library Place" `in Jersey` TRUE `a private dwelling house` FALSE `with an activity` TRUE) `and the principal address entered` NOTHING) EQUALS LIST "10 Library Place"
-- Several: the eligible ones, in order.
#ASSERT `Art 8(3)(d) the addresses of other premises in Jersey to be entered` (`facts with other premises` (LIST `premises at` "1 Hill Street" `in Jersey` TRUE `a private dwelling house` FALSE `with an activity` TRUE, `premises at` "2 Elm Close" `in Jersey` TRUE `a private dwelling house` TRUE `with an activity` TRUE, `premises at` "4 Quay Street" `in Jersey` TRUE `a private dwelling house` FALSE `with an activity` TRUE) `and the principal address entered` (JUST "10 Library Place")) EQUALS LIST "1 Hill Street", "4 Quay Street"
#ASSERT `Art 8(3)(d) the addresses of other premises in Jersey to be entered` `no further facts for Article 8(3)` EQUALS EMPTY

§§ `Article 8(3)(h) to (n): the conditional items`

`Alpha, an organized religious charity` MEANS
    `Registered charity` WITH
        entity IS `a company in the general section`
        `registration number` IS "C-0002"
        `registered name` IS "Alpha Charity Limited"
        `alternative registered names` IS EMPTY
        `date registered` IS YMD 2019 3 1
        `date deregistered` IS NOTHING
        `registered charitable purposes` IS LIST "the advancement of religion"
        `registered public benefit statement` IS "Worship is held in public and the hall is open to all"
        `is an organized religious charity` IS TRUE

#ASSERT `Art 8(3)(h) a note that the charity is an organized religious charity is required` `Alpha, an organized religious charity`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 8(3)(h) a note that the charity is an organized religious charity is required` `Alpha, registered on 1 March 2019`

#ASSERT `Art 8(3)(i) the text of the provision in the constitution is required` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Art 8(3)(i) the text of the provision in the constitution is required` FALSE

#ASSERT `Art 8(3)(m) the details or statement under the Order are required` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Art 8(3)(m) the details or statement under the Order are required` FALSE

-- (k): a notice served on the charity on 10 January 2024 and complied with, and one served on a governor on 5 March 2025 and not complied with.
`a notice served on the charity and complied with` MEANS
    `Required steps notice` WITH
        `served on` IS `the registered charity`
        `prompted by` IS `there has been misconduct by a registered charity`
        `date served` IS YMD 2024 1 10
        `steps to be taken by` IS JUST (YMD 2024 3 1)
        `requires a governor to be suspended, removed or replaced` IS FALSE
        `has been complied with` IS TRUE

`a notice served on a governor and not complied with` MEANS
    `Required steps notice` WITH
        `served on` IS `a governor of the registered charity`
        `prompted by` IS `a governor of a registered charity has engaged in misconduct`
        `date served` IS YMD 2025 3 5
        `steps to be taken by` IS NOTHING
        `requires a governor to be suspended, removed or replaced` IS FALSE
        `has been complied with` IS FALSE

`both notices` MEANS LIST `a notice served on the charity and complied with`, `a notice served on a governor and not complied with`

-- F3.8: the favoured reading notes every notice served, the other only a notice not complied with.
#ASSERT `Art 8(3)(k) the required steps notices to be noted` fav `both notices` EQUALS `both notices`
#ASSERT `Art 8(3)(k) the required steps notices to be noted` `interpretation F3.8 reading B` `both notices` EQUALS LIST `a notice served on a governor and not complied with`
#ASSERT `Art 8(3)(k) the required steps notices to be noted` `interpretation F3.8 reading B` (LIST `a notice served on the charity and complied with`) EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `Art 8(3)(k) the required steps notices to be noted` fav (LIST `a notice served on the charity and complied with`) EQUALS LIST `a notice served on the charity and complied with`
#ASSERT `Art 8(3)(k) the required steps notices to be noted` fav EMPTY EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `Art 8(3)(k) the required steps notices to be noted` `interpretation F3.8 reading B` EMPTY EQUALS EMPTY

GIVEN names IS A LIST OF STRING
GIVETH A `Facts for the items of Article 8(3)`
`facts with previous names` names MEANS
    `Facts for the items of Article 8(3)` WITH
        `other premises` IS EMPTY
        `principal address entered` IS NOTHING
        `previous registered names` IS names
        `information prescribed by an Order under Article 8(3)(n)` IS EMPTY

GIVEN info IS A LIST OF STRING
GIVETH A `Facts for the items of Article 8(3)`
`facts with information prescribed by Order` info MEANS
    `Facts for the items of Article 8(3)` WITH
        `other premises` IS EMPTY
        `principal address entered` IS NOTHING
        `previous registered names` IS EMPTY
        `information prescribed by an Order under Article 8(3)(n)` IS info

-- (l): "if the registered name has been changed, the previous registered name or names".
#ASSERT `Art 8(3)(l) the previous registered names to be entered` (`facts with previous names` (LIST "Alpha Aid", "Alpha Relief")) EQUALS LIST "Alpha Aid", "Alpha Relief"
#ASSERT `Art 8(3)(l) the previous registered names to be entered` `no further facts for Article 8(3)` EQUALS EMPTY

-- (n): "any other information prescribed by the Minister by Order": required if an Order prescribes some.
#ASSERT `Art 8(3)(n) other information prescribed by the Minister by Order is required` (`facts with information prescribed by Order` (LIST "the charity's website"))
#ASSERT NOT `Art 8(3)(n) other information prescribed by the Minister by Order is required` `no further facts for Article 8(3)`

§§ `Article 8(3): the items required for a registered charity`

-- The names of the entries, for the expected lists.
`item (a)` MEANS `a note of the status of the entity`
`item (b)` MEANS `the names of each of the governors`
`item (c)` MEANS `the principal address`
`item (d)` MEANS `the address of any other premises in Jersey`
`item (e)` MEANS `the registered charitable purposes`
`item (f)` MEANS `the registered public benefit statement`
`item (g)` MEANS `the date on which the charity was registered`
`item (h)` MEANS `a note that the charity is an organized religious charity`
`item (i)` MEANS `the text of the provision in the constitution that falls within Article 5(2)`
`item (j)` MEANS `whether the charity has or has not sent its annual return for the most recent year`
`item (k)` MEANS `a note of a required steps notice and of the date on which it was served`
`item (l)` MEANS `the previous registered names`
`item (m)` MEANS `the details or statement that must be entered under an Order under Article 13(9)(c)`
`item (n)` MEANS `other information prescribed by the Minister by Order`

-- Always required: (a), (b), (c), (e), (f), (g), (j).
`the seven items always required` MEANS LIST `item (a)`, `item (b)`, `item (c)`, `item (e)`, `item (f)`, `item (g)`, `item (j)`

GIVEN charity IS A `Registered charity`
      f5 IS A BOOLEAN
      notices IS A LIST OF `Required steps notice`
      f13 IS A BOOLEAN
      facts IS A `Facts for the items of Article 8(3)`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Entry required by Article 8(3)`
`the entries required, on the favoured readings, for` charity `with the Article 5(3) fact` f5 `the notices` notices `the Article 13(9) fact` f13 `and the facts` facts MEANS
    `Art 8(3) the entries required for the registered charity` fav charity f5 notices f13 facts

#ASSERT `the entries required, on the favoured readings, for` `Alpha, registered on 1 March 2019` `with the Article 5(3) fact` FALSE `the notices` EMPTY `the Article 13(9) fact` FALSE `and the facts` `no further facts for Article 8(3)` EQUALS `the seven items always required`
-- The restricted section too: "whether entered in the general or restricted section".
#ASSERT `the entries required, on the favoured readings, for` `Alpha, registered on 1 March 2019 and entered in the restricted section` `with the Article 5(3) fact` FALSE `the notices` EMPTY `the Article 13(9) fact` FALSE `and the facts` `no further facts for Article 8(3)` EQUALS `the seven items always required`
-- (d) alone.
#ASSERT `the entries required, on the favoured readings, for` `Alpha, registered on 1 March 2019` `with the Article 5(3) fact` FALSE `the notices` EMPTY `the Article 13(9) fact` FALSE `and the facts` (`facts with other premises` (LIST `premises at` "1 Hill Street" `in Jersey` TRUE `a private dwelling house` FALSE `with an activity` TRUE) `and the principal address entered` (JUST "10 Library Place")) EQUALS LIST `item (a)`, `item (b)`, `item (c)`, `item (d)`, `item (e)`, `item (f)`, `item (g)`, `item (j)`
-- (h) alone.
#ASSERT `the entries required, on the favoured readings, for` `Alpha, an organized religious charity` `with the Article 5(3) fact` FALSE `the notices` EMPTY `the Article 13(9) fact` FALSE `and the facts` `no further facts for Article 8(3)` EQUALS LIST `item (a)`, `item (b)`, `item (c)`, `item (e)`, `item (f)`, `item (g)`, `item (h)`, `item (j)`
-- (i) alone.
#ASSERT `the entries required, on the favoured readings, for` `Alpha, registered on 1 March 2019` `with the Article 5(3) fact` TRUE `the notices` EMPTY `the Article 13(9) fact` FALSE `and the facts` `no further facts for Article 8(3)` EQUALS LIST `item (a)`, `item (b)`, `item (c)`, `item (e)`, `item (f)`, `item (g)`, `item (i)`, `item (j)`
-- (k) alone.
#ASSERT `the entries required, on the favoured readings, for` `Alpha, registered on 1 March 2019` `with the Article 5(3) fact` FALSE `the notices` `both notices` `the Article 13(9) fact` FALSE `and the facts` `no further facts for Article 8(3)` EQUALS LIST `item (a)`, `item (b)`, `item (c)`, `item (e)`, `item (f)`, `item (g)`, `item (j)`, `item (k)`
-- (l) alone.
#ASSERT `the entries required, on the favoured readings, for` `Alpha, registered on 1 March 2019` `with the Article 5(3) fact` FALSE `the notices` EMPTY `the Article 13(9) fact` FALSE `and the facts` (`facts with previous names` (LIST "Alpha Aid")) EQUALS LIST `item (a)`, `item (b)`, `item (c)`, `item (e)`, `item (f)`, `item (g)`, `item (j)`, `item (l)`
-- (m) alone.
#ASSERT `the entries required, on the favoured readings, for` `Alpha, registered on 1 March 2019` `with the Article 5(3) fact` FALSE `the notices` EMPTY `the Article 13(9) fact` TRUE `and the facts` `no further facts for Article 8(3)` EQUALS LIST `item (a)`, `item (b)`, `item (c)`, `item (e)`, `item (f)`, `item (g)`, `item (j)`, `item (m)`
-- (n) alone.
#ASSERT `the entries required, on the favoured readings, for` `Alpha, registered on 1 March 2019` `with the Article 5(3) fact` FALSE `the notices` EMPTY `the Article 13(9) fact` FALSE `and the facts` (`facts with information prescribed by Order` (LIST "the charity's website")) EQUALS LIST `item (a)`, `item (b)`, `item (c)`, `item (e)`, `item (f)`, `item (g)`, `item (j)`, `item (n)`
-- All fourteen.
#ASSERT `the entries required, on the favoured readings, for` `Alpha, an organized religious charity` `with the Article 5(3) fact` TRUE `the notices` `both notices` `the Article 13(9) fact` TRUE `and the facts` `facts for every conditional item` EQUALS LIST `item (a)`, `item (b)`, `item (c)`, `item (d)`, `item (e)`, `item (f)`, `item (g)`, `item (h)`, `item (i)`, `item (j)`, `item (k)`, `item (l)`, `item (m)`, `item (n)`
-- F3.8 reading B: the notice complied with is not noted, so (k) stays if a notice is outstanding and goes if none is.
#ASSERT `Art 8(3) the entries required for the registered charity` `interpretation F3.8 reading B` `Alpha, registered on 1 March 2019` FALSE `both notices` FALSE `no further facts for Article 8(3)` EQUALS LIST `item (a)`, `item (b)`, `item (c)`, `item (e)`, `item (f)`, `item (g)`, `item (j)`, `item (k)`
#ASSERT `Art 8(3) the entries required for the registered charity` `interpretation F3.8 reading B` `Alpha, registered on 1 March 2019` FALSE (LIST `a notice served on the charity and complied with`) FALSE `no further facts for Article 8(3)` EQUALS `the seven items always required`
-- Not a registered charity: no item is required by Article 8(3) (the historic section is Article 8(5)'s).
#ASSERT `the entries required, on the favoured readings, for` `Alpha, registered on 1 March 2019 and deregistered on 1 June 2024` `with the Article 5(3) fact` FALSE `the notices` EMPTY `the Article 13(9) fact` FALSE `and the facts` `no further facts for Article 8(3)` EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `the entries required, on the favoured readings, for` (`the register record of` `a company that applies` `registered on` (YMD 2019 3 1) `and deregistered on` NOTHING) `with the Article 5(3) fact` FALSE `the notices` EMPTY `the Article 13(9) fact` FALSE `and the facts` `no further facts for Article 8(3)` EQUALS EMPTY

`facts for every conditional item` MEANS
    `Facts for the items of Article 8(3)` WITH
        `other premises` IS LIST `premises at` "1 Hill Street" `in Jersey` TRUE `a private dwelling house` FALSE `with an activity` TRUE
        `principal address entered` IS JUST "10 Library Place"
        `previous registered names` IS LIST "Alpha Aid"
        `information prescribed by an Order under Article 8(3)(n)` IS LIST "the charity's website"

-- The duty: the Commissioner must enter each required item.  Seven items for the plain charity; the trace enters all seven (in a different order from the Article's).
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 8(3) the Commissioner must enter in the register the entries required for the registered charity` fav `Alpha, registered on 1 March 2019` FALSE EMPTY FALSE `no further facts for Article 8(3)` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `enter in the register an item required in respect of a registered charity` `item (g)` AT 1
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `enter in the register an item required in respect of a registered charity` `item (a)` AT 2
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `enter in the register an item required in respect of a registered charity` `item (b)` AT 3
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `enter in the register an item required in respect of a registered charity` `item (c)` AT 4
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `enter in the register an item required in respect of a registered charity` `item (e)` AT 5
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `enter in the register an item required in respect of a registered charity` `item (f)` AT 6
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `enter in the register an item required in respect of a registered charity` `item (j)` AT 7

-- One item still to enter: the duty stands.
-- EXPECT: STANDING | MUST `enter in the register an item required in respect of a registered charity`
#TRACE `Art 8(3) the Commissioner must enter in the register the entries required for the registered charity` fav `Alpha, registered on 1 March 2019` FALSE EMPTY FALSE `no further facts for Article 8(3)` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `enter in the register an item required in respect of a registered charity` `item (a)` AT 2
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `enter in the register an item required in respect of a registered charity` `item (b)` AT 3
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `enter in the register an item required in respect of a registered charity` `item (c)` AT 4
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `enter in the register an item required in respect of a registered charity` `item (e)` AT 5
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `enter in the register an item required in respect of a registered charity` `item (f)` AT 6
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `enter in the register an item required in respect of a registered charity` `item (g)` AT 7

-- An entity that is not a registered charity: nothing is required, so the duty is already discharged.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 8(3) the Commissioner must enter in the register the entries required for the registered charity` fav `Alpha, registered on 1 March 2019 and deregistered on 1 June 2024` FALSE EMPTY FALSE `no further facts for Article 8(3)` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 5)

§§ `Article 8(3): the items missing from a register entry`

`the note of a company` MEANS
    `Note of status recorded in the register (Article 8(3)(a))` WITH
        `sub-paragraphs of Article 2(1) recorded` IS LIST `kind (f)`
        `whether it also falls within sub-paragraph (a), as recorded` IS JUST FALSE
        `details of the enactment, Act of the States, Royal Charter, Act of the United Kingdom Parliament, Order in Council or foreign law` IS NOTHING

GIVEN note IS A MAYBE `Note of status recorded in the register (Article 8(3)(a))`
      names IS A LIST OF STRING
      address IS A MAYBE STRING
      purposes IS A BOOLEAN
      benefit IS A BOOLEAN
      annual IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Entry in the register for a registered charity (Article 8(3))`
`an entry for Alpha with the note` note `the names` names `the principal address` address `the purposes approved` purposes `the benefit statement approved` benefit `and the annual return` annual MEANS
    `Entry in the register for a registered charity (Article 8(3))` WITH
        `the registered charity` IS `Alpha, registered on 1 March 2019`
        `note of status` IS note
        `names of the governors` IS names
        `principal address` IS address
        `addresses of other premises in Jersey` IS EMPTY
        `statement of purposes approved by the Commissioner` IS purposes
        `public benefit statement approved by the Commissioner` IS benefit
        `note of the organized religious charity and of the provision of the Order` IS NOTHING
        `text of the provision of the constitution within Article 5(2)` IS NOTHING
        `annual return sent for the most recent year` IS annual
        `notes of required steps notices` IS EMPTY
        `previous registered names` IS EMPTY
        `details or statement under an Order under Article 13(9)(c)` IS NOTHING
        `other information prescribed by Order` IS EMPTY

`a complete entry for Alpha` MEANS `an entry for Alpha with the note` (JUST `the note of a company`) `the names` (LIST "Ann Le Brun", "Bob Renouf") `the principal address` (JUST "10 Library Place") `the purposes approved` TRUE `the benefit statement approved` TRUE `and the annual return` (JUST TRUE)

GIVEN e IS AN `Entry in the register for a registered charity (Article 8(3))`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Entry required by Article 8(3)`
`the items missing from` e MEANS `Art 8(3) the items missing from the register entry` fav e FALSE EMPTY FALSE `no further facts for Article 8(3)`

#ASSERT `the items missing from` `a complete entry for Alpha` EQUALS EMPTY


-- Each of the seven items, taken out one at a time.
#ASSERT `the items missing from` (`an entry for Alpha with the note` NOTHING `the names` (LIST "Ann Le Brun", "Bob Renouf") `the principal address` (JUST "10 Library Place") `the purposes approved` TRUE `the benefit statement approved` TRUE `and the annual return` (JUST TRUE)) EQUALS LIST `item (a)`
#ASSERT `the items missing from` (`an entry for Alpha with the note` (JUST `the note of a company`) `the names` (LIST "Ann Le Brun") `the principal address` (JUST "10 Library Place") `the purposes approved` TRUE `the benefit statement approved` TRUE `and the annual return` (JUST TRUE)) EQUALS LIST `item (b)`
#ASSERT `the items missing from` (`an entry for Alpha with the note` (JUST `the note of a company`) `the names` (LIST "Ann Le Brun", "Bob Renouf") `the principal address` NOTHING `the purposes approved` TRUE `the benefit statement approved` TRUE `and the annual return` (JUST TRUE)) EQUALS LIST `item (c)`
-- (e) is entered only once the Commissioner has approved it as accurately reflecting the constitution; (f) likewise.
#ASSERT `the items missing from` (`an entry for Alpha with the note` (JUST `the note of a company`) `the names` (LIST "Ann Le Brun", "Bob Renouf") `the principal address` (JUST "10 Library Place") `the purposes approved` FALSE `the benefit statement approved` TRUE `and the annual return` (JUST TRUE)) EQUALS LIST `item (e)`
#ASSERT `the items missing from` (`an entry for Alpha with the note` (JUST `the note of a company`) `the names` (LIST "Ann Le Brun", "Bob Renouf") `the principal address` (JUST "10 Library Place") `the purposes approved` TRUE `the benefit statement approved` FALSE `and the annual return` (JUST TRUE)) EQUALS LIST `item (f)`
-- (j) records "has or has not sent": a recorded "has not" is entered; only NOTHING is a missing entry.
#ASSERT `the items missing from` (`an entry for Alpha with the note` (JUST `the note of a company`) `the names` (LIST "Ann Le Brun", "Bob Renouf") `the principal address` (JUST "10 Library Place") `the purposes approved` TRUE `the benefit statement approved` TRUE `and the annual return` NOTHING) EQUALS LIST `item (j)`
#ASSERT `the items missing from` (`an entry for Alpha with the note` (JUST `the note of a company`) `the names` (LIST "Ann Le Brun", "Bob Renouf") `the principal address` (JUST "10 Library Place") `the purposes approved` TRUE `the benefit statement approved` TRUE `and the annual return` (JUST FALSE)) EQUALS EMPTY
-- A note of the wrong status is a missing (a).
#ASSERT `the items missing from` (`an entry for Alpha with the note` (JUST `a note of a trust`) `the names` (LIST "Ann Le Brun", "Bob Renouf") `the principal address` (JUST "10 Library Place") `the purposes approved` TRUE `the benefit statement approved` TRUE `and the annual return` (JUST TRUE)) EQUALS LIST `item (a)`
-- Several at once, in the Article's order.  Item (g), the date of registration, is a field the register record always has, so it is never missing.
#ASSERT `the items missing from` (`an entry for Alpha with the note` NOTHING `the names` EMPTY `the principal address` NOTHING `the purposes approved` FALSE `the benefit statement approved` FALSE `and the annual return` NOTHING) EQUALS LIST `item (a)`, `item (b)`, `item (c)`, `item (e)`, `item (f)`, `item (j)`

-- Item (k): each notice to be noted needs a note of it AND of the date on which it was served, for the same recipient.
GIVEN notes IS A LIST OF `Note of a required steps notice (Article 8(3)(k))`
GIVETH AN `Entry in the register for a registered charity (Article 8(3))`
`an entry for Alpha noting` notes MEANS
    `Entry in the register for a registered charity (Article 8(3))` WITH
        `the registered charity` IS `Alpha, registered on 1 March 2019`
        `note of status` IS JUST `the note of a company`
        `names of the governors` IS LIST "Ann Le Brun", "Bob Renouf"
        `principal address` IS JUST "10 Library Place"
        `addresses of other premises in Jersey` IS EMPTY
        `statement of purposes approved by the Commissioner` IS TRUE
        `public benefit statement approved by the Commissioner` IS TRUE
        `note of the organized religious charity and of the provision of the Order` IS NOTHING
        `text of the provision of the constitution within Article 5(2)` IS NOTHING
        `annual return sent for the most recent year` IS JUST TRUE
        `notes of required steps notices` IS notes
        `previous registered names` IS EMPTY
        `details or statement under an Order under Article 13(9)(c)` IS NOTHING
        `other information prescribed by Order` IS EMPTY

GIVEN served IS A `Recipient of a required steps notice`
      date IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Note of a required steps notice (Article 8(3)(k))`
`a note of a notice served on` served `on` date MEANS
    `Note of a required steps notice (Article 8(3)(k))` WITH
        `served on` IS served
        `date served` IS date
        `note or copy of the notice` IS "a copy of the notice"

GIVEN e IS AN `Entry in the register for a registered charity (Article 8(3))`
      notices IS A LIST OF `Required steps notice`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Entry required by Article 8(3)`
`the items missing from` e `given the notices` notices MEANS `Art 8(3) the items missing from the register entry` fav e FALSE notices FALSE `no further facts for Article 8(3)`

#ASSERT `the items missing from` (`an entry for Alpha noting` (LIST (`a note of a notice served on` `a governor of the registered charity` `on` (YMD 2025 3 5)))) `given the notices` (LIST `a notice served on a governor and not complied with`) EQUALS EMPTY
-- A note of the right recipient with another date, or of the right date for another recipient, or no note: item (k) is missing.
#ASSERT `the items missing from` (`an entry for Alpha noting` (LIST (`a note of a notice served on` `a governor of the registered charity` `on` (YMD 2025 3 6)))) `given the notices` (LIST `a notice served on a governor and not complied with`) EQUALS LIST `item (k)`
#ASSERT `the items missing from` (`an entry for Alpha noting` (LIST (`a note of a notice served on` `the registered charity` `on` (YMD 2025 3 5)))) `given the notices` (LIST `a notice served on a governor and not complied with`) EQUALS LIST `item (k)`
#ASSERT `the items missing from` (`an entry for Alpha noting` EMPTY) `given the notices` (LIST `a notice served on a governor and not complied with`) EQUALS LIST `item (k)`
-- Two notices: both must be noted.
#ASSERT `the items missing from` (`an entry for Alpha noting` (LIST (`a note of a notice served on` `a governor of the registered charity` `on` (YMD 2025 3 5)))) `given the notices` `both notices` EQUALS LIST `item (k)`
#ASSERT `the items missing from` (`an entry for Alpha noting` (LIST (`a note of a notice served on` `a governor of the registered charity` `on` (YMD 2025 3 5)), (`a note of a notice served on` `the registered charity` `on` (YMD 2024 1 10)))) `given the notices` `both notices` EQUALS EMPTY
-- No notice served: no note is needed.
#ASSERT `the items missing from` (`an entry for Alpha noting` EMPTY) `given the notices` EMPTY EQUALS EMPTY
